module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_join_between_supporting_records_stands_in_for_a_join_to_the_active_instance

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

// A claim about ONE running thing (one arrival run, one write, one controller) is discharged by checking
// that SEVERAL RECORDS about that thing agree WITH EACH OTHER. Agreement between records is not identity to
// the active instance: a pair can be perfectly consistent and still belong to another run, another
// controller, or another moment. Nothing in the shape of the records says which instance they are of, so the
// check passes for the wrong reason and the claim reads green.
data a_join_between_supporting_records_stands_in_for_a_join_to_the_active_instance: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_join_between_supporting_records_stands_in_for_a_join_to_the_active_instance" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "**a relation asserted BETWEEN supporting records is accepted as a relation to the ACTIVE instance the claim names** (INVALID STATE: a guard that must hold of one run's own write, or of one controller's own readings, is written as a cross-comparison of records that merely describe a write or a controller. gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_converge admit_forced_first_rotation_precedes_prior_life compared the sealed forced state carried by the pending against the sealed forced state carried by the admitted write -- two seals over one story, equal by construction -- while never asking whether the pending was minted under THIS run's AccessDiscover step instance, whether the write's attempt is THIS run's intake attempt, or whether the controller the forced state, the route standing and the post-write account observation name is the controller the run's own access read names. Its positive control mixed identities and still converged: srv13's write, run_a's run, mtjade1's subject, reads and archive.)",
    "THE SAME SHAPE WITHOUT ANY IDENTITY INVOLVED -- ORDERING ASSERTED BY THE CALLER (INVALID STATE: a boundary that must show one effect happened between two observations takes an instant the caller supplies and an archive the caller LABELS pre-write, instead of deriving the order from the sealed instants the observers stamped. gunbc.machine_intake.prior_life_boundary PriorLifeForcedWriteContext carried a caller write_instant: EpochMs and an optional pre_write_archive; a genuine archive read AFTER the write, passed in under the pre-write name, established the boundary over a history the write may have erased -- the exact case the indeterminate outcome exists to stop. The archive's own sealed read_at, which already travels with it, said otherwise.)",
    "HARM. The guard is satisfied by a pair that agrees, so it cannot fail when the pair is foreign: an arrival run takes a divergence row that places a write before a standing on the strength of an admission made under another run's attempt or at another controller's address, and a prior-life boundary establishes across a write whose ordering nobody observed. Both are silent -- every field is well-formed, every seal is valid, and the fold converges. The damage is not a wrong answer at the guard but the guard's whole purpose: the row exists to admit an effect out of phase order ONLY for the one unit, in the one run, under the one build that produced the evidence.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. refusal_reason_minted_as_canonical_identity is a value from the WRONG vocabulary in a name's place; a_binding_position_recorded_as_a_declaring_identity is a value from the RIGHT vocabulary read at the WRONG LAYER. This row is neither: every record is well-formed, correctly sealed, and mutually consistent. The missing fact is IDENTITY AND ORDER WITH RESPECT TO THE ACTIVE INSTANCE -- which run minted it, which controller it describes, whether it sits before or after an effect -- and no comparison among the records can supply it, because the records do not name the instance. The recognition rule is a question about the CHECK, not the data: for every guard of the form 'these records must agree', ask what would happen if the whole set were replaced by a consistent set from another run or controller -- if the answer is 'the guard still passes', the guard is not the one the claim names.",
    "RECEIPT (2026-10-31, proud-bat-605, found by the side chat's REQUEST_CHANGES on gunbc#15372 at fa5831d, P1-a and P1-b). REPAIRED by joining to the active instance and by deriving order from sealed observer instants: the classifier now requires the pending's step instance to BE this run's AccessDiscover instance (step_instance_key_eq), the write's attempt to equal intake_attempt_of_run(run), the endpoint to be shared across the forced state, the route standing, this run's access read and this run's BMC observation, the BMC observation's subject and attempt to be the write's, and the write transition's application to name the same subject; the boundary takes no caller instant and no labelled archive at all -- it derives the order from the archive's sealed read_at against the write leg's own begin and completion (forced_first_rotation_write_leg, produced through convergence_fold's effect_leg_deadline and complete_effect_leg), and refuses when the pre-capture is not ordered before the leg. DISCRIMINATORS, measured at the repair and red without it: machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness w_a_matching_forced_pair_from_another_run_cannot_take_the_row and w_a_matching_forced_pair_for_another_controller_cannot_take_the_row (both sides agree with each other; the run or the controller is foreign), and machine_intake_prior_life_boundary_witness w_a_post_write_archive_passed_as_the_pre_capture_does_not_establish (a genuine post-write archive passed under the pre-write name yields the typed indeterminate, not establishment). The positive control was rewritten so that one unit and one run produce every record (srv13_forced_write_sequence: the 403, the account read, the plan, the write leg, the dry apply and the authenticated readback from one sequence of the real producers).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent wrongness. The fold converged, the witness passed, and the guard it exercised was a different guard.",
    "CEILING: structurally impossible today. A step instance key, an intake attempt and an observer-stamped instant are all carriers a foreign record CAN inhabit; the join is enforced per fact, at each use site, and a new driver can re-decide it by cross-comparison. What would close it is a carrier for 'this run's active instance' that a record from another run cannot inhabit -- the same wall a_binding_position_recorded_as_a_declaring_identity names from the identity side.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: an active-instance carrier in gunbc.fleet.convergence_fold (a run-scoped identity a supporting record cannot be minted under), so admit_callers or the fold itself refuses a foreign record at the boundary rather than at a use site; until then the enrolled claims above are the wall and are permanent regression controls, not expecting-red probes.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_converge", decl_name: "admit_forced_first_rotation_precedes_prior_life", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.prior_life_boundary", decl_name: "dry_archive_prior_life_across_forced_write", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.prior_life_boundary", decl_name: "forced_first_rotation_write_leg", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_a_matching_forced_pair_from_another_run_cannot_take_the_row", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_a_matching_forced_pair_for_another_controller_cannot_take_the_row", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_prior_life_boundary_witness", decl_name: "w_a_post_write_archive_passed_as_the_pre_capture_does_not_establish", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
